{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,320p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && printf '\\\\n--- existing review area ---\\\\n' && find reviews -maxdepth 2 -type f -print | sort | xargs -r -n1 sh -c 'echo --- \\\"\"'$0\"; sed -n \"1,220p\" \"$0\"'\"' && printf '\\\\n--- candidate tracking files ---\\\\n' && find AristotleCandidates -maxdepth 2 -type f -print | sort | sed -n '1,200p' && printf '\\\\n--- project config ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,200p' lakefile.lean\"","aggregated_output":"# Aristotle CLI reference\n\n## Setup\n\n- Install: `uv tool install aristotlelib`\n- Verify: `aristotle --version`\n- Authenticate: set `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` in the shell environment, or use the skill wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\nIf the key is stored near the end of `~/.bashrc`, noninteractive commands may not see it because many `.bashrc` files contain:\n\n```bash\ncase $- in\n    *i*) ;;\n      *) return;;\nesac\n```\n\nIn that case, do not rely on `source ~/.bashrc`. Use the wrapper, which reads a literal `export ARISTOTLE_API_KEY=...` assignment without printing it:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize input.md\n```\n\n## Core commands\n\nSubmit a Lean project for sorry filling or proof search:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh submit \"Fill in all sorries\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\nFormalize a TeX or paper source:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize paper.tex --wait --destination output.tar.gz\n```\n\nList recent jobs:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh list --limit 10\n```\n\nDownload a completed job:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh download <project-id> --destination result.tar.gz\n```\n\nPass the key directly for one command only:\n\n```bash\naristotle submit \"My prompt\" --api-key \"$ARISTOTLE_API_KEY\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\n## Recommended project loop\n\n1. Inspect the Lean project locally.\n2. Run the narrowest local build or test that exercises the target files.\n3. Submit a focused Aristotle prompt against the project directory.\n4. Wait for the run if the expected result is a concrete patch.\n5. Download or inspect the produced artifact.\n6. Rebuild locally and repeat with a tighter prompt if needed.\n\n## Prompt shape\n\nKeep prompts short and file-bound. Good prompts mention:\n\n- the exact project directory\n- the theorem or file to work on\n- whether to fill `sorry`s, formalize a statement, or debug a failing proof\n- what counts as a useful partial result\n\nAvoid vague prompts such as \"improve this project\" unless the scope is intentionally broad.\n\n--- existing review area ---\n\n--- candidate tracking files ---\nAristotleCandidates/BicommutantVonNeumannCore.lean\nAristotleCandidates/BoundedStateGNS.lean\nAristotleCandidates/CStarAlphaGNSBridge.lean\nAristotleCandidates/CStarCompletionAlphaInterface.lean\nAristotleCandidates/CStarGNSBridge.lean\nAristotleCandidates/CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility.lean\nAristotleCandidates/CStarTracialWeightCore.lean\nAristotleCandidates/CStarTransport.lean\nAristotleCandidates/ConcreteCStarCompletion.lean\nAristotleCandidates/ConstructedAlgebraicAlpha.lean\nAristotleCandidates/DensityPartialTrace.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarEquiv.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateEquivCoherence.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateFactorization.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteCoordinateMapNormControl.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteDensityMatrix.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteModelSanity.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FinitePauliOrthogonality.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteProductStateCoherence.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FinitePureFactor.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteStabilizerDimension.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteStabilizerProductState.lean\nAristotleCandidates/FiniteStabilizerProjector.lean\nAristotleCandidates/GNSCommutantConjugation.lean\nAristotleCandidates/GNSUnitaryIntertwiner.lean\nAristotleCandidates/InfiniteAlgebraicRegionalEquiv.lean\nAristotleCandidates/InfiniteAlgebraicStateTransport.lean\nAristotleCandidates/LayeredDirectLimit.lean\nAristotleCandidates/NormalVonNeumannExtensionInterface.lean\nAristotleCandidates/OneQubitPartialTrace.lean\nAristotleCandidates/PreGNSIsometry.lean\nAristotleCandidates/RegionalWitness.lean\n\n--- project config ---\nimport Lake\nopen Lake DSL\n\npackage «stabilizerHyperfiniteFormalization» where\n\nrequire mathlib from git\n  \"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4.git\" @ \"v4.28.0\"\n\nlean_lib Formalization where\n\nlean_lib AristotleCandidates where\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
